    "intro_html":  "Gumbo is a roux dish first and everything else second. You stir flour and fat over heat until it turns the color of an old penny, and that dark roux is where the flavor, the color, and the whole identity of the pot come from. Skip it, rush it, or scorch it and you do not have gumbo, you have soup. Take your time and you get 562 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e46 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e per bowl for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.88 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
